  "alt": "A large frame labelled SOFTWARE FACTORY contains process design above and tolerance below. The upper dashed band shows a left-to-right path: engineering intent, context / work, fabricator, realization. An annotation below the path names what process design determines: context, tools, routing, authority, and sequencing. The fabricator is one station in the process. Below, a TOLERANCE heading defines acceptable product variation beside a pale-gray bounded ACCEPTABLE REGION. Four black dots mark distinct acceptable realizations. An arrow from realization reaches the region; its measurement annotation lists tests, property-based testing, analysis, simulation, and human judgment. Two arrows leave the region: outside leads to revise / reject, and within tolerance leads to admitted change.",
